{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 36, :comments ["<b>Interest and increase.</b> The Sages treated them as one, and one transgresses by two negative prohibitions (Bava Metzia 60)." "<b>And you shall fear your Elohim.</b> Because a person's mind is drawn after interest, and it is hard to refrain from it, and he rationalizes to himself permission for his money that was sitting idle with him — it was necessary to say ״וְיָרֵאתָ מֵאֱלֹהֶיךָ״. Or one who lends his money to a gentile in order to lend it to an Israelite at interest — this is a matter delivered over to a person's heart and thought; therefore it was necessary to say ״וְיָרֵאתָ מֵאֱלֹהֶיךָ״ (ibid. 61b)."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:08:28.888971222Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}